# QuickXP GitHub roadmap tracking

Roadmap work is tracked on GitHub for [freitagdavid/QuickXP](https://github.com/freitagdavid/QuickXP).

## Sources of truth

1. **Product intent:** [`docs/ROADMAP.md`](docs/ROADMAP.md) (mirrored in [`.cursor/plans/xp_shell_gap_analysis.plan.md`](.cursor/plans/xp_shell_gap_analysis.plan.md)).
2. **Tickets / progress:** GitHub Issues + the **QuickXP Roadmap** project.
3. **Issue number map:** [`docs/github-roadmap-map.json`](docs/github-roadmap-map.json) (regenerated by the sync script).

## When the user asks to complete a roadmap task

1. Identify the matching issue (by title, epic label, or `docs/github-roadmap-map.json`).
2. Work against that issue: reference `#N` in commits/PR; update issue status when done.
3. On completion: close the feature issue (or set `status:done` / close if already closed for done items), comment a short summary, and update the parent epic if the epic is now complete or only partial.
4. Keep [`docs/ROADMAP.md`](docs/ROADMAP.md) checkboxes/status text aligned with what shipped (mark `[x]` / note partial).
5. Re-run or update sync so the project board matches: `python3 scripts/sync-roadmap-github.py` (idempotent; skips existing titles).

## When the roadmap changes

If you add, remove, rename, or re-scope epics/features in `docs/ROADMAP.md`:

1. Update `build_items()` in [`scripts/sync-roadmap-github.py`](scripts/sync-roadmap-github.py) to match.
2. Run `python3 scripts/sync-roadmap-github.py` so new issues are created and the project is refreshed.
3. Refresh `docs/github-roadmap-map.json` (the script writes it).
4. For renamed/removed items: close obsolete issues with a comment pointing at the replacement; do not leave the board stale.

## Conventions

- Epic issues: `Epic X — …` with label `roadmap:epic` + `epic:X`.
- Feature issues: `[Epic X] …` with `roadmap:feature` + `epic:X` + `status:*`.
- Backlog: `[Backlog] …` with `roadmap:backlog`.
- Status labels: `status:todo` | `status:partial` | `status:done` (done features are closed).
- Prefer one GitHub Project (**QuickXP Roadmap**) for the shell epic board unless the user asks for more boards.
